    "narrative": "For June 24, 2026, **Brice Turang** stands as our highest-value play with a 75.06 efficiency score, buoyed significantly by a favorable matchup against a starter with a 5.10 xERA. The combination of his top-third lineup placement and the high projected SP vulnerability makes him an auto-start. Joining him in the elite tier are **Tyler Soderstrom** (66.55) and **Corbin Carroll** (65.91). While **Corbin Carroll** faces a decent arm in Liberatore, his elite sprint speed remains the engine of our category-scarcity strategy, and **Tyler Soderstrom** benefits from an assumed #4 order slot and favorable wind conditions that could turn fly balls into HR production. **James Wood** rounds out our must-starts; despite facing a tougher matchup against Nola, his elite 0.404 xwOBA profile and leadoff positioning keep his score firm at 60.72.\n\nThe bench decision process was tightly contested, specifically regarding **Zach McKinstry**. He finished with a 47.70 score\u2014just shy of our preferred thresholds\u2014but ultimately fell behind **Kyle Karros** due to a more favorable park factor. While **Zach McKinstry** offered a platoon edge, the optimization favored the broader base projection and lineup security of the active starters. Meanwhile, prospects like **Dalton Rushing**, **Alex Freeland**, and **Cole Young** remain on the outside looking in, all posting sub-40 scores primarily due to unfavorable matchups against high-skill arms like Ryan and Ashcraft.\n\nOwners should remain vigilant regarding lineup volatility. Both **Max Muncy** and **Tyler Soderstrom** have \"Lineup Pending\" status; if **Max Muncy** is pushed further down the order than the assumed #9 slot, his efficiency\u2014already hampered by a 51.28 score\u2014could dip toward our floor. We are also monitoring the risk associated with **Austin Riley** and **Jose Caballero**, who are tasked with navigating elite arms in Sears and Skubal, respectively. While **Jose Caballero** maintains a strong platoon-driven boost, his outcome is highly sensitive to Skubal\u2019s dominance; he remains a calculated risk to ensure we don't leave potential SB production on the bench.",
